WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.044 --> 00:00:01.051
- It's a hillbilly way of saying

00:00:01.051 --> 00:00:04.190
back that thing up, or bootylicious.

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.440
(intense guitar music)

00:00:10.431 --> 00:00:13.848
(funky electronic music)

00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:17.659
- Should be interesting.

00:00:17.659 --> 00:00:19.257
- Probably about trucks and beer.

00:00:19.257 --> 00:00:21.159
- Hopefully they're not
too against country.

00:00:21.159 --> 00:00:22.064
Well, let's see what we got here.

00:00:22.064 --> 00:00:23.893
- Buzzfeed, take one.

00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:26.665
- Does every great country
star grow up on a farm?

00:00:26.665 --> 00:00:27.498
No.

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:29.146
- No. That's so funny!

00:00:29.146 --> 00:00:32.466
- I didn't grow up on a
farm, so yes, so maybe yes.

00:00:32.466 --> 00:00:33.995
- I grew up in southern California.

00:00:33.995 --> 00:00:35.615
Country music spans the whole globe,

00:00:35.615 --> 00:00:37.460
and it could come from anywhere.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.020
- What does Honky Tonk Badonkadonk mean?

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.726
Well, this is somebody
that knows country music.

00:00:43.726 --> 00:00:44.816
- Booty!

00:00:44.816 --> 00:00:47.589
♫ Honky tonk badonkadonk.

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:49.839
- A well-proportioned butt.

00:00:51.187 --> 00:00:52.368
- Is there a single dirt road ...

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:53.319
(laughing)

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.496
- Is there a single dirt
road every country star

00:00:55.496 --> 00:00:58.342
has to visit before writing a song?

00:00:58.342 --> 00:00:59.654
- That is a great question.

00:00:59.654 --> 00:01:02.103
Yes, there's this one specific
dirt road in Nashville.

00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:04.042
It's about two miles south of town.

00:01:04.042 --> 00:01:06.306
- No, any old dirt road will do.

00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:09.371
- You sing a lot about
being down by the river.

00:01:09.371 --> 00:01:12.239
Is it better than being down by the beach?

00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:13.696
- The river is pretty fun, especially

00:01:13.696 --> 00:01:16.323
when you're younger and
you don't live by a beach.

00:01:16.323 --> 00:01:19.218
- I am from Florida, so
I have many more songs

00:01:19.218 --> 00:01:22.076
about being by the beach
than I do being by the river.

00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:23.911
- Why does every country
song have to mention

00:01:23.911 --> 00:01:27.609
a tractor, beer, boots,
or kicking up the hay?

00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:29.121
What the hell are you listening to?

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.562
- See, that's what people think!

00:01:30.562 --> 00:01:32.155
- I'm sure I'm wrong, but I've never heard

00:01:32.155 --> 00:01:33.913
the expression "kicking up the hay."

00:01:33.913 --> 00:01:35.173
- There's a lot of songs
about tractors, beer, boots.

00:01:35.173 --> 00:01:36.386
Those are great songs too.

00:01:36.386 --> 00:01:38.035
There's actually more to it than that.

00:01:38.035 --> 00:01:41.311
- Somebody needs to die,
somebody needs to get laid,

00:01:41.311 --> 00:01:42.879
and you gotta say
something about your mama.

00:01:42.879 --> 00:01:45.612
Those are things that are
in every country song.

00:01:45.612 --> 00:01:46.655
- Why whiskey?

00:01:46.655 --> 00:01:47.509
- Why not?

00:01:47.509 --> 00:01:49.059
- Because whiskey is awesome.

00:01:49.059 --> 00:01:51.129
- Like if it gives you that
weird warm feeling inside.

00:01:51.129 --> 00:01:52.672
- Hey man, we're gonna go out there, man,

00:01:52.672 --> 00:01:55.494
hit the old pinot noir, and
do a little two steppin'.

00:01:55.494 --> 00:01:56.911
It just doesn't sound right, does it?

00:01:56.911 --> 00:01:58.984
- Does Jesus always
have to take the wheel?

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.705
- Well, I sure hope he does if
I start to have an accident.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:03.453
- Well, if he's in your life ...

00:02:03.453 --> 00:02:05.137
- Yeah, and if you've been drinking ...

00:02:05.137 --> 00:02:07.703
- I'd rather have Jesus take
the wheel than anybody I know.

00:02:07.703 --> 00:02:09.560
- Does Jesus always
have to take the wheel?

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.616
No, that's up to you.

00:02:10.616 --> 00:02:12.175
- Do any of your songs mention a cat

00:02:12.175 --> 00:02:15.757
or are you really all just dog people?

00:02:15.757 --> 00:02:17.542
- Oh, I could answer that so many ways.

00:02:17.542 --> 00:02:18.799
- I am a dog person.

00:02:18.799 --> 00:02:21.071
- You don't think of a cat
being loyal and wonderful.

00:02:21.071 --> 00:02:23.153
Dogs are very loyal creatures.

00:02:23.153 --> 00:02:24.763
- And I just don't like cats,

00:02:24.763 --> 00:02:26.580
so I can't speak for the
rest of country music.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.072
- All you non-country fans out there,

00:02:28.072 --> 00:02:29.523
I guess that's like maybe two of you.

00:02:29.523 --> 00:02:31.422
- We're a good blend of
everything right now.

00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:34.307
I pull from all the top 40 hip hop songs,

00:02:34.307 --> 00:02:35.857
pull from all the classic rock stuff.

00:02:35.857 --> 00:02:38.983
- We aren't all singing
about picking up chicks

00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:40.657
and putting them in the truck bed.

00:02:40.657 --> 00:02:42.728
I don't really think it would
make sense for me to do that.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:44.779
- If you like lyrics about real people

00:02:44.779 --> 00:02:47.815
and real situations, maybe
you should listen to it.

00:02:47.815 --> 00:02:49.224
- I found country music because

00:02:49.224 --> 00:02:51.124
I had an older sister who hated it.

00:02:51.124 --> 00:02:53.904
One day, trying to be an
annoying little brother,

00:02:53.904 --> 00:02:56.231
I turned it on and Tim
McGraw "Don't Take the Girl"

00:02:56.231 --> 00:02:58.734
came on, and I fell in
love with country music.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.450
I don't know what the natural
inclination to push back

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.309
against country music
is, but it's timeless

00:03:03.309 --> 00:03:05.398
and it's not going
away, so give it a shot.

00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:07.378
- Those were funny questions actually.

00:03:07.378 --> 00:03:10.325
I actually have those same questions.

00:03:10.325 --> 00:03:12.908
(bubbly music)

